# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions for the SECONDO regression suite.
#
# Every entry below is a REAL finding that was measured, not a false positive.
# They are suppressed so UBSan can run with halt_on_error=1 and still fail the
# suite on anything NEW. This list is a ratchet: work it down, do not add to
# it. When a finding is fixed, delete its line and the suite will keep it fixed.
#
# Measured from a full 'run-tests.sh -tty' pass on a UBSan build, 2026-08-19.
# The count is how many test suites hit it, i.e. how much of the suite each one
# is currently costing.
#
# Format is <check>:<source file>. Note this suppresses the check for the whole
# file, not just the line named, so a fix is always better than an entry here.

# 10 suites -- uninitialised bool in the attribute type descriptor
bool:AttrType.h

# 1 suite -- uninitialised bool read in Attribute
bool:Attribute.h

# 1 suite -- third-party header, not our code
bool:librip.h

# 6 suites -- misaligned int32_t load in the storage key encoding
alignment:smiKey.cpp

# 3 suites -- invalid KeyDataType enum value in the ordered-relation key path
enum:CompositeKey.cpp

# 1 suite -- misaligned unsigned long load
alignment:TrajectoryAnnotation.cpp

# 1 suite -- misaligned float store
alignment:Vertex.cpp

# 1 suite -- 46341 * 46341 overflows int
signed-integer-overflow:StandardAlgebra.cpp

# 1 suite -- subtracting LLONG_MIN overflows long int
signed-integer-overflow:DateTimeAlgebra.cpp

# 1 suite -- left shift of 16777216 by 24 places overflows int
shift-base:Import.h

# 1 suite -- member call through a null R_Tree pointer
null:JNetwork.cpp

# 1 suite -- variable length array with a non-positive bound
vla-bound:Collection.cpp

# --- found by a later full pass; same backlog, same rules ---

# 3 suites -- member call through a misaligned R_Tree pointer
alignment:NetworkAlgebra.cpp

# 1 suite -- invalid TimeType enum value
enum:DateTimeAlgebra.cpp

# 1 suite -- invalid ERoadType enum value
enum:ONetworkAdapter.h

# NOT suppressed, on purpose: FileIndexAlgebra places Attribute and Rectangle
# objects directly into unaligned on-disk page buffers, so every field access
# on one is reported. That is ~130 findings in FileIndex.examples from a single
# root cause -- the page buffers need aligning (or the objects need copying
# through an aligned temporary). It is left failing because 185 of those
# reports land in core headers (Attribute.h, StandardTypes.h,
# RectangleAlgebra.h); suppressing those would switch off alignment checking
# for the whole tree to silence one algebra.
